prop teomsg obj.name=teomsg
prop councilgate obj.name=councilgate
prop verdictauthority obj.name=verdictauthority
prop verdictfleet obj.name=verdictfleet
prop verdictunion obj.name=verdictunion
prop verdictexpose obj.name=verdictexpose
prop verdictfree obj.name=verdictfree

note bulletin Storm bulletin | HARBOR AUTHORITY - STORM BULLETIN\n\nGale tonight. Shutters down on every roof. The alarm bell on the Authority's roof to be rung when it breaks.\n\nThe council meets in the storm, as the law says. The Authority, the Fleet and the Union will each be heard.
note authdemand Authority demand | THE AUTHORITY'S DEMAND\n\nThe water stays with those who keep the pumps. The Fleet's smuggling ends. The Union's tenth is raised to a fifth.\n\nOrder keeps the city dry.
note fleetdemand Fleet demand | THE FREE FLEET'S DEMAND\n\nThe pumps to the boats that carry the water. The Authority's permits burned. The boom open, day and night.\n\nThe sea belongs to those who sail it.
note uniondemand Union demand | THE UNION'S DEMAND\n\nThe Union's divers brought up every pump in this city. The pumps are ours by salvage law.\n\nWhat we bring up, we share - with the Union.
note authsecret Authority secret | Sealed with the Authority's anchor -\n\nCouncillor Crane: the Fleet and the Union were paid to countersign. If this comes out, all three go down together. Keep the code safe: it starts 4.
note fleetsecret Fleet secret | Sealed with the Fleet's gull -\n\nTeo: we took the Authority's money for the valves. The boats needed fuel. The Rookery will never know. The code's middle: 7 then 1.
note unionsecret Union secret | Sealed with the Union's hook -\n\nForeman: Marlowe's dive was meant to find the pumps, not the valves. If she talks, we are finished. The code ends 9.
note letters Faction letters | The factions' letters for the council, sealed and stacked - one each, and none of them meant for you.
note fiveways Five ways | FIVE WAYS THE CITY CAN GO\n\nTHE AUTHORITY - order, and the water stays theirs.\nTHE FLEET - the pumps go to the boats.\nTHE UNION - salvage law; the cranes rule.\nEXPOSE - read the valve log aloud; let the city judge all three.\nFREE - the water goes to the Rookery, and the Rookery leaves for a shoal of its own.\n\nPull one lever. The council will hear only one.
note verdictauthority The verdict | THE AUTHORITY KEEPS THE WATER.\n\nThe pumps stay locked. The streets stay quiet. In the Rookery the barrels stay empty, and nobody asks why.
note verdictfleet The verdict | THE FLEET TAKES THE PUMPS.\n\nBoats come and go through an open boom. The water flows - to whoever has a boat.
note verdictunion The verdict | THE UNION RUNS THE WATER.\n\nThe cranes turn day and night. Every barrel filled is chalked, every chalk mark paid.
note verdictexpose The verdict | ALL THREE EXPOSED.\n\nThe valve log is read in every market. The councillor runs, the Fleet's captains scatter, the foreman resigns. The city will have to start again.
note verdictfree The verdict | THE ROOKERY GOES FREE.\n\nThe Rookery's barrels are filled from the Authority's tanks, and at dawn its boats leave for a shoal of their own, ahead of you to the south.
note teomsg Teo Varga's message | Left on the council table, in the Fleet's chalk -\n\nWhatever you chose, I am not staying to see it. The valves were my shame.\n\nThere's a signal from the south, on the old Concord band - the builders of the pumps. I'm sailing toward it. Follow if you like.\n\n- Teo Varga
note pilemap Pile engineer's map | THE FOUNDATION PILES\n\nThe whole crown stands on four piles. The storm has cracked them. Jack them up, one by one, or the city goes down tonight.\n\nThe stair at the west shore goes down to the first pile head.
note councilchest Council reward | The council's reward, for the one who spoke.
loot letters Rope*2
prop letters loot.refill=0
loot councilchest TradeToken*10;MetalIngot*4;CircuitBoard*2
prop councilchest loot.refill=0

